### Minor — T11-F1-M1: component capture command example omits its required mode

File: docs/evidence/audit-remediation-20260927/r01-forward/task-11-evidence.md:172.

The documented command is `bun docs/evidence/audit-remediation-20260927/r01-forward/task-11-component-capture.ts OWNOUT`, but the wrapper checks argv[2] equals `component` at task-11-component-capture.ts:3 and reads the output from argv[3] at :4. Copying the stated command fails with `Exact component capture mode required` before capture. Correct the example to:

`bun docs/evidence/audit-remediation-20260927/r01-forward/task-11-component-capture.ts component OWNOUT`

This is a documentary handoff defect, not a defect in the actual source/proof execution. Correct prose through the same implementer, retain executed/raw historical receipts, and bind the resulting metadata-only closing SHA. No DB/application gate rerun is justified for that prose-only change.

